    <div class="proj-copy">
      <div class="proj-number">02 · UX/UI Design · Eplan</div>
      <h2>Testing Lab*</h2>
      <p class="proj-subtitle">Breaking down the wall between product teams and the people actually using the software.</p>

      <div class="proj-block">
        <div class="proj-block-label">The Problem</div>
        <p>Product development at scale suffers from a familiar blind spot: the people building the software rarely see how it's used in the wild. Eplan wanted to change that — not just internally, but by inviting customers into the process too. The question was how to design a space that felt genuinely collaborative, not performative.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="proj-block">
        <div class="proj-block-label">What I did</div>
        <p>I kicked off the project with a design thinking workshop, then moved straight into user interviews — making sure real needs shaped the concept before any design decisions were made. The output was a collaborative cloud platform: a digital playground for product updates, idea exchange, and feature testing — accessible to customers, employees, and dev teams alike.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="proj-block">
        <div class="proj-block-label">Ongoing</div>
        <p>The first wireframes and prototypes were validated with end-users. The project continued to evolve — a platform built to grow as the community around it grows.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="nda-notice">
